sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2, superseding the Pass 1 audit. The fixed-patch model is unchanged: onset wavelength 3.101 µm for D. virilis, 2.924 µm for D. teissieri, and no selected wavenumber for D. willistoni, all at 0 Ma. Dispersion Pearson r remains 0.998 (RMSE 0.032). The new domain-length series, at fixed dx = 0.5 µm, counts 4, 6, and 13 midline activator peaks on patches of 16, 32, and 48 µm. The count rises with length; the spacing is not constant (4.33, 5.00, 3.625 µm), so this is mode insertion in the weak sense, not a clean L/λ doubling. The habitus Nyquist length remains 7.76 µm and is now printed on the comparison figure as a negative result. Overall 87.8/100 (faithfulness 87.4, reproducibility 88.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 87, Reproducibility package 89. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_virilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 571020 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 3547b4f69ff07d6a09765a5200342289ad1ed2fce47e1421ce033bb56b597924 (sha256 3547b4f69ff07d6a09765a5200342289ad1ed2fce47e1421ce033bb56b597924), spec_fingerprint 7b617b1b25587059791fa537573c287d828ce4628df471d7ad0d187921f12af8. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7b617b1b25587059791fa537573c287d828ce4628df471d7ad0d187921f12af8; artifact_sha256: 3547b4f69ff07d6a09765a5200342289ad1ed2fce47e1421ce033bb56b597924. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical-wavenumber selection from the dispersion relation of a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics and the steady state u0 = a + b, v0 = b/(a+b)^2. | Gompel et al. 2005: abdominal pigment differences among Drosophila species are cis-regulatory, including posterior bands in the melanogaster subgroup. | Hanson 2019 CC BY-SA 4.0 lateral habitus of Drosophila virilis (Wikimedia File:Dvir 1-2.jpg).; reconstructed_in_script: Du solved so virilis onset λ_c = 3.101 µm at Dv/Du = 10 and b = 0.90. | Teissieri a = 0.058 and willistoni a = 0.360 as the chronoseries step at fixed age and fixed diffusivities. | Tergite mode counts from project atlas adult lengths divided by seven. | Adult GIF endpoint is the habitus photograph modulated by the normalized PDE field.; transfer_boundary: The 3.101 µm target is the slot scale. It is not a published ocellus measurement for D. virilis. | Atlas body lengths are used only to turn a wavelength into a mode count.; does_not_claim: That the habitus photograph resolves a 3.1 µm pigment wavelength (measured Nyquist is 7.76 µm). | That willistoni lost a Turing pattern through geological time (successor is extant, 0 Ma). | That chorion-filament number enters the wavenumber law. | That the PDE generated the wing veins or the body outline.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [specimen_comparison/morphometric-validation, pressure P=3.0]: One lateral habitus. Pixel scale cannot confirm the 3.101 µm mode.",
            "remediation needed: R1 closed. domain_length_series counts 4, 6, and 13 midline peaks at 16, 32, and 48 µm. Spacing is 4.33, 5.00, and 3.625 µm, so the count rises without a locked wavelength.",
            "remediation needed: R2 closed as a negative result. Nyquist length 7.76 µm is measured, asserted in --self-test, and printed on the habitus panel. The photograph does not resolve 3.101 µm.",
            "remediation needed: R3 still open. Basal activator levels remain a reconstruction from pigmentation class, not a fit to a measured concentration series.",
            "remediation needed: R4 still open. One assessor." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.878"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

